# Shell preferences

- **Bash over PowerShell:** The maintainer uses Git Bash on Windows. Always propose Bash commands and scripts (e.g. `./scripts/foo.sh`), never PowerShell. Git Bash is installed with Git and is the preferred shell for this project on Windows; the same Bash scripts run on Linux and macOS.
- **On Windows, avoid bare `bash` when launching from another shell:** `bash` may resolve to `C:\Windows\System32\bash.exe` (WSL) instead of Git Bash.
- **Mandatory launcher rule (Windows):** from PowerShell/CMD/agent shells, always invoke Bash through the explicit Git for Windows binary:
	- `& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc '<command>'`
- **WSL guardrail:** never use `C:\Windows\System32\bash.exe` for repo scripts. If `Get-Command bash` resolves to System32, do not use bare `bash`; use the explicit Git Bash path above.
- **Quick identity check (when in doubt):**
	- `& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc 'command -v bash; uname -a'`
	- Expected shell family includes `MINGW`/`MSYS`, not `Linux` from WSL.
- **Maven baseline:** `./scripts/build.sh` from Git Bash is the single canonical Java validation entrypoint on all platforms. From PowerShell (e.g. Cursor agent shell), use `& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc './scripts/build.sh'`. Do not introduce or rely on `.cmd` / `.bat` build wrappers.
- **Avoid Windows-only script formats** (`.cmd`, `.bat`, `.ps1`) for repo tooling unless there is no portable Bash equivalent. Prefer one Bash script that works on Windows (Git Bash), Linux, and macOS.
- **Known keepers (do not purge casually):** Android `ezkey_mobile/android/gradlew.bat` (Gradle wrapper); interim mobile Maestro harnesses under `ezkey_mobile/scripts/*.ps1` until that orthogonal workstream ports them.
